# PART M — PERFORMANCE AND RELIABILITY

## 19. OPTIMIZE FOR A HACKATHON

This project must be realistic to develop within a short hackathon.

Therefore:

- Use primitive geometry rather than complicated models.
- Avoid unnecessary graphics libraries.
- Reuse components.
- Keep the scene lightweight.
- Avoid creating new AI requests every animation frame.
- Use a single configurable LLM provider initially.
- Keep prompts compact.
- Cache or summarize relevant history.
- Use asynchronous backend requests.
- Make API calls resilient to failure.
- Ensure all gameplay works without a language model.
- Prefer clear, modular code over complicated abstractions.

### AI performance

Avoid making every AI generate a response whenever the human speaks.

Select one relevant speaker most of the time.

When an AI needs to act, attempt to obtain its decision and optional dialogue in one model request.

Separate conversation responses and poker actions only when necessary.

### Recovery

If an external AI provider fails:

- Record an internal error.
- Use legal fallback behaviour.
- Continue the game.
- Avoid freezing the interface.

If microphone support is unavailable, allow typed dialogue instead.

